      "id": "les-miserables-s182-p01901",
      "source_en": "called Little Gavroche. Why was he called Little Gavroche? Probably because his father’s name was Jondrette. It seems to be the instinct of certain wretched families to break the thread. The chamber which the Jondrettes inhabited in the Gorbeau hovel was the last at the end of the corridor. The cell next to it was occupied by a very poor young man who was called M. Marius. Let us explain who this M. Marius was.",
